==== Serial ====

{{:media:tenda:w306r_serialpoints.jpg?200|Photo of PCB with markings}}

In order to de-brick, or install OpenWrt using Method 1, you will need to connect a serial cable to the device. You will need to [[docs:techref:hardware:soldering|solder]] wires to a header, then connect [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial.cables]] device to communicate to the serial port of a computer.

**In Version 2.0:** The pads to solder to are near the CPU on the underside of the circuit board.\\

The serial settings needed are:
| Rate           | 57600   |
| Data Bits      | 8       |
| Stop Bits      | 1       |
| Parity         | none    |
| Flow Control   | none    |

-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.

